hypotheses.statement:
For each $q$, let $\mathscr A_q$ be a deterministic class of pairs $(D,C)$ as above. Assume there is $a>0$ such that every pair in every class has either $m=0$ or $m\ge aq$. Suppose every subsequential limit <a href="#eq:profile-limits" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:profile-limits">[eq:profile-limits]</a>, along objects in the classes with $q\to\infty$, satisfies $$\label{eq:visible-excess}
 \nu_D(\text{$D$-visible profiles})+
 \nu_C(\text{$C$-visible profiles})>c.$$ There is $b>0$ such that, for all sufficiently large $q$, $$\mathsf U_{q,k}\{D:\text{some }C\text{ has }(D,C)\in\mathscr A_q\}
 \le \exp(-bq\log q).$$ The constants may depend on $k,a$ and the sequence of classes.

Fix constants $c_*,C_*>0$ and $0<c_0\le1$, and put $\beta=1/8$. For each sufficiently large integer $q$, let a finite graph have its vertex set partitioned into $n=2(q+1)$ slots $Q_i$, with no edge within a slot. Write $N(v)$ for the neighborhood of a vertex. Suppose that $$\begin{aligned}
 c_*q\le |Q_i|\le q,&\qquad |N(v)|\le C_*q,
 \qquad |N(v)\cap Q_i|\le q^\beta,\label{sel:graph-bounds}\\
 |J(v)|\le q^\beta,&\qquad
 |N(v)\cap N(w)|\le q^\beta\quad(w\notin J(v)),\label{sel:exceptional}
\end{aligned}$$ where every $w\in J(v)$ is either adjacent to $v$ or in its slot. There are constants $K_*,\rho>0$, depending only on $c_*,C_*,c_0$, and a random procedure which either fails or returns an independent transversal $(V_i)_{i\in I_0}$, where $I_0$ is the set of slots and $V_i\in Q_i$. If $\mathcal A$ denotes its event of returning a transversal, then $$\label{sel:success}
 \mathbb P(\mathcal A)=1-o(1).$$ For any $s$ distinct slots $i_1,\ldots,i_s$ and any prescribed vertices $v_j\in Q_{i_j}$, $$\label{sel:cylinder}
 \mathbb P\bigl(\mathcal A, V_{i_j}=v_j\ (1\le j\le s)\bigr)
 \le (K_*/q)^s.$$

